<section class="section wrap" id="about"><div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow small">01 / About me</div><h2>Learning by building.</h2></div><p>A practical, project-first approach to learning the tools behind reliable software delivery.</p></div><div class="about-grid"><article class="panel reveal"><h3>My approach</h3><p>I’m working toward an entry-level DevOps / Cloud role. My focus is understanding the full delivery path: source control, build automation, packaging, containers, deployment, and troubleshooting. I aim to document what I build and keep improving through practice.</p></article><div class="terminal reveal"><div class="terminal-head"><span class="win-dot"></span><span class="win-dot"></span><span class="win-dot"></span><span style="margin-left:8px">tejas@devops-lab:~</span></div><div class="terminal-body"><div class="terminal-line"><span class="prompt">tejas@lab</span>:~$ whoami</div><div class="terminal-line term-cyan">Tejas Sushanth H V</div><div class="terminal-line"><span class="prompt">tejas@lab</span>:~$ cat focus.txt</div><div class="terminal-line term-violet" id="typedText">Linux, Git, Docker, CI/CD, cloud fundamentals</div><div class="terminal-line"><span class="prompt">tejas@lab</span>:~$ <span class="cursor"></span></div></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="skills"><div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow small">02 / Toolkit</div><h2>Skills I’m developing.</h2></div><p>Keep this list aligned with the tools you can explain and demonstrate in an interview.</p></div><div class="skill-grid reveal"><div class="skill"><i>01</i> Linux & Shell</div><div class="skill"><i>02</i> Git & GitHub</div><div class="skill"><i>03</i> Docker</div><div class="skill"><i>04</i> Jenkins</div><div class="skill"><i>05</i> Maven</div><div class="skill"><i>06</i> Apache Tomcat</div><div class="skill"><i>07</i> CI/CD pipelines</div><div class="skill"><i>08</i> YAML</div><div class="skill"><i>09</i> AWS fundamentals</div><div class="skill"><i>10</i> GitHub Actions</div><div class="skill"><i>11</i> Networking basics</div><div class="skill"><i>12</i> Troubleshooting</div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="projects"><div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow small">03 / Selected work</div><h2>Projects, not just buzzwords.</h2></div><p>Use these cards to document your real implementation, screenshots, repository links, and lessons learned.</p></div><div class="grid-3"><article class="project-card reveal" data-tilt><div class="project-number">PROJECT / 01</div><h3>Java WAR deployment</h3><p>Package a Java web application with Maven, deploy the WAR to Tomcat, and validate the running endpoint.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Java</span><span class="tag">Maven</span><span class="tag">Tomcat</span><span class="tag">WAR</span></div></article><article class="project-card reveal" data-tilt><div class="project-number">PROJECT / 02</div><h3>Dockerized web app</h3><p>Build a container image in a multi-stage Dockerfile and run the app with a mapped host port.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Docker</span><span class="tag">Containers</span><span class="tag">Tomcat</span></div></article><article class="project-card reveal" data-tilt><div class="project-number">PROJECT / 03</div><h3>CI/CD automation</h3><p>Extend the project pipeline to checkout source, run a Maven build, archive the WAR, and publish build status.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Jenkins</span><span class="tag">Git</span><span class="tag">Maven</span></div></article><article class="project-card reveal" data-tilt><div class="project-number">PROJECT / 04</div><h3>Linux operations lab</h3><p>Practice users and groups, permissions, services, logs, process checks, disk usage, and shell scripting in Ubuntu.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Ubuntu</span><span class="tag">Bash</span><span class="tag">Systemd</span></div></article><article class="project-card reveal" data-tilt><div class="project-number">PROJECT / 05</div><h3>GitHub Actions workflow</h3><p>Create a workflow that builds the project on push and pull requests, then retains build artifacts for review.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">GitHub Actions</span><span class="tag">YAML</span><span class="tag">CI</span></div></article><article class="project-card reveal" data-tilt><div class="project-number">NEXT UP / 06</div><h3>Infrastructure as Code</h3><p>Planned learning project: define a small cloud environment using Terraform, variables, outputs, and a safe teardown process.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">Terraform</span><span class="tag">Cloud</span><span class="tag">Planned</span></div></article></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="journey"><div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow small">04 / Journey</div><h2>Experience & certifications.</h2></div><p>This section is intentionally honest and editable: add verified work history and certificates as you earn them.</p></div><div class="timeline"><article class="panel reveal"><div class="eyebrow small">Hands-on learning</div><h3>DevOps & Cloud project practice</h3><p>Building and troubleshooting small deployments with Linux, Git, Maven, Docker, Jenkins, and Tomcat. Add dates and measurable outcomes as your work grows.</p><span class="tag">Project-based learning</span></article><article class="panel reveal"><div class="eyebrow small">Certifications</div><h3>Certifications & coursework</h3><p>No certification claims are pre-filled. Add the exact certificate name, issuing organization, date, and credential link after completion.</p><span class="tag">Update with verified credentials</span></article></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="github"><div class="section-head reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow small">05 / Open source</div><h2>GitHub activity.</h2></div><p>Connect your real GitHub profile to showcase repositories, commits, and hands-on progress.</p></div><div class="panel github-panel reveal"><div><div class="gh-icon">⌘</div><h3>Code, learn, repeat.</h3><p>My GitHub profile link is a placeholder until you add your exact username. Replace it in this page and in the README so recruiters can browse your repositories.</p></div><a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open GitHub ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="contact"><div class="contact-box reveal"><div><div class="eyebrow small">06 / Contact</div><h2>Let’s build something reliable.</h2><p>I’m interested in entry-level DevOps and Cloud opportunities where I can contribute, learn from experienced engineers, and grow through real delivery work.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;margin-top:12px">Before publishing, replace the placeholder email and profile links in this page.</p></div><div class="actions" style="margin-top:0"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:your.email@example.com">Email me ↗</a><a class="btn btn-quiet" href="assets/Tejas-Sushanth-HV-Resume.txt" download>Resume ↓</a></div></div></section></main>
